//
// loft#934 — the PASS-1 half of `934-unresolved-name-reports-itself.loft`.
//
// Both diagnostics here are emitted during pass 1, so they abort before pass 2 runs.  Kept
// in their own file for the reason the `36`/`36b` and `102`/`102b` pairs are split: a
// single pass-1 error silences every `!first_pass` diagnostic in the same file, and its
// annotations then assert nothing while the suite stays green (loft#929).
//
// Both are CONTROLS for the loft#934 fix rather than symptoms of it — each names a report
// the fix had to leave alone.  See the companion file for the eleven pass-2 rows.

// A name given a written type ANNOTATION is reported by `resolve_deferred_unknown`, not by
// the bare-value site the fix added.  Reporting in both places is one typo and two errors,
// which is why the new report is scoped to a stub pass 1 registered on SPECULATION.
// @EXPECT_ERROR: Undefined type PeAnnotation
fn pe_annotation_still_reports() {
  y: PeAnnotation = null;
  println("{y}");
}

// A genuine retype still reports.  `never` is the poison an already-reported expression
// leaves behind, and suppressing the retype message for it must not reach a type the
// author actually wrote — `y = 1; y = "s"` is the reader's own mistake, and `as` is the
// right instrument for it.
// @EXPECT_ERROR: Variable 'y' cannot change type from integer to text
fn pe_real_retype() {
  y = 1;
  y = "s";
  println("{y}");
}
